-- title:
--   Systems of parameters in Cohen–Macaulay local rings are regular
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$. Assume that $R$ is Cohen–Macaulay in the sense that $\operatorname{depth}_R R = \dim R$ as elements of $\mathbb{N}_\infty$ adjoined a bottom element, where $\operatorname{depth}_R R$ is defined as the supremum of the lengths of those lists $s$ of elements of $R$ which form a weakly regular sequence on $R$ and all of whose entries lie in $\mathfrak m$, and $\dim R$ is the Krull dimension `ringKrullDim R`. Assume further that $\dim R = d$ for a natural number $d$, and let $xs$ be a list of elements of $R$ of length exactly $d$, all of whose entries lie in $\mathfrak m$, such that the quotient of $R$ by the ideal generated by the entries of $xs$ has Krull dimension $0$. The conclusion is that $xs$ is a regular sequence on $R$ in the sense of `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular`: it is weakly regular, i.e. the $i$-th entry acts injectively on the quotient of $R$ by the ideal generated by the preceding entries, and in addition $R$ is not equal to the ideal generated by the entries of $xs$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that in a Cohen–Macaulay Noetherian local ring every system of parameters is a regular sequence (Matsumura, Theorem 17.4(iii)). It is used in the project to produce regular sequences for flatness criteria over regular local rings and in the finite-freeness computations for quotients arising from formal group power series.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isRegular_of_systemOfParameters.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Patching_SystemTypes

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open IsLocalRing RingTheory

theorem IsLocalRing.isRegular_of_systemOfParameters
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (hCM : (Module.depth R R : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim R)
    {d : ℕ} (hdim : ringKrullDim R = d)
    (xs : List R) (hlen : xs.length = d) (hmem : ∀ y ∈ xs, y ∈ maximalIdeal R)
    (hsop : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ Ideal.ofList xs) = 0) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R xs := by sorry
